{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPEFq4p1YjK5CaEWGy6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I graded F9 **\"true, not planted\"** (no problem id) and saved `grade.json`.\n\nThe finding doesn't match any of the six planted problems, but the truth tables confirm it:\n\n- **Clocked hours are accurate.** In every year from 2016 to 2025, clocked hours were 1.006 to 1.008 times the true operation hours (t404). So the analyst's clocked-hours measure was sound.\n- **The real work fell while paid hours held.** True operation hours went from 121,721 h in 2016 and 117,890 h in 2017 to 106,265 h in 2025 (t404). The growing unclocked paid time is real spare capacity, as the finding says.\n- **The 2016 drop was real efficiency.** True hours per estimated hour fell within 2016: laser from 0.989 to 0.807 and brake from 1.057 to 0.855, January to December. Over the same months, clocked hours stayed at 1.00 to 1.01 times true hours (t405). That answers the question the analyst left open: it was not a change in how labour was booked.\n\nI didn't recompute the analyst's dollar size ($255,110 a year). It rests on clocked hours, which the truth shows are accurate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":26535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630},"output_tokens":395,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3aa46655-26dd-4894-836a-b721a515c721","uuid":"de6afb16-2307-49fa-b917-292ada0ac44f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:56:51.082Z","request_id":"req_011CgPEFpnhEg8P3y7FP221W"}
